---
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy Direction | HarborNavi</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="HarborNavi privacy direction for the harbornavi.com early access list."
    />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://harbornavi.com/privacy" />
  </head>
  <body data-route="privacy">
    <SiteHeader activeRoute="privacy" />
    <main>
      <section class="privacy-page section-shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy direction</p>
        <h1>HarborNavi is being designed for local-first home video AI.</h1>
        <p>
          This page explains the privacy direction for HarborNavi early access and will be updated as the product
          moves closer to launch.
        </p>
        <div class="privacy-grid">
          <article>
            <h2>Useful events first</h2>
            <p>
              HarborNavi is intended to help households choose useful events, review alerts, and save selected
              moments without turning every camera frame into another notification.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>No default cloud video promise</h2>
            <p>
              The product direction is local-first. HarborNavi should not require default cloud upload of raw home
              video, broad identification, or emergency response behavior.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Waitlist data</h2>
            <p>
              The early access form may ask for email, country, camera setup, main interest, beta willingness, and
              one free-text pain point. A fuller retention policy will be published before broader launch.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer">
      <span>HarborNavi</span>
      <a href="/home">Home</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
